From 0c2a6c67385779d580fb6946efcb36eaf18e5908 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HuJK <gh@hujk.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:03:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] user client: take an input IOKit passed out of line (over
 4096 bytes) by its descriptor alone

is_io_connect_method points structureInput at the (empty) inband buffer even when the input came out
of line, so the test `!structureInput && structureInputDescriptor` never held: every tunnel call
longer than 4096 bytes fell through to the selector table and came back kIOReturnUnsupported. Those
are virtgpu EXECBUFFERs of a heavy frame (over ~83 command buffers in one submission -- the wallpaper
editor, Stage Manager); Turnip took the refusal for a lost device ("submit failed: 0xe00002c7"),
and Core Animation ended backboardd, a respring each time. The out-of-line path is now taken when
there is a descriptor and no inband bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MmgVbdYzu7uPjUcpLVQMTq
(cherry picked from commit 32e864ad7cb0ffd4a12c8c6854450c5046c7bc8d)
---
 NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp b/NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp
index 929154f..1eeba11 100644
--- a/NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp
+++ b/NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp
@@ -524,8 +524,12 @@ IOReturn AGXDeviceUserClient::externalMethod(uint32_t selector,IOExternalMethodA
      * so which selector numbers reach this object is decided outside the driver. A tunnel call carries the real ABI method in its
      * first eight bytes and may use ANY admitted selector: {magic, method, payload...} in, the method's exact output out. Method
      * 0xffffffff is a probe that only proves the selector was admitted. */
-    /* An input longer than IOKit passes inline (4096 bytes: a virtgpu command) arrives as memory of the caller's: read it here. */
-    if(arguments && !arguments->structureInput && arguments->structureInputDescriptor) {
+    /* An input longer than IOKit passes inline (4096 bytes: a virtgpu command) arrives as memory of the caller's: read it here. Its
+     * structureInput is NOT null then (is_io_connect_method points it at the empty inband buffer, structureInputSize 0): testing it
+     * for null refused every such command as an unknown selector, kIOReturnUnsupported -- a submission of a heavy frame (over ~83
+     * command buffers: the wallpaper editor, Stage Manager), which Turnip took for a lost device, and Core Animation then ended
+     * backboardd. */
+    if(arguments && arguments->structureInputDescriptor && !arguments->structureInputSize) {
         IOMemoryDescriptor *memory=arguments->structureInputDescriptor;
         const IOByteCount size=memory->getLength();
         if(size<8 || size>NativeAdrenoTunnelMaxInput)return kIOReturnBadArgument;
